<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil says fire out at Dartmouth.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil says fire out at Dartmouth.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said on Friday that emergency crews extinguished a fire at its Dartmouth, Nova Scotia refinery that began at about 2230 local time on Thursday.</p>
<p>Imperial said there were no injuries. The fire was contained within the Vacuum Tower, a unit that distills crude into its separate components. The unit was shut down on October 4 for maintenance and was therefore not processing crude.</p>
<p>The cause and the extent of any damage would be investigated, Imperial said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
